    ('Water Main Access Cover', 'Find circular metal covers marked with "W" or water company initials, usually blue in color or with blue trim, located along streets and sidewalks.', 'Find a circular or square metal cover set flush in street or sidewalk bearing text labels ''WATER MAIN'' or water utility markings with bolt holes around perimeter.', 'common'::public.item_rarity, 'Water main covers are often marked with symbols or text indicating the utility; many cities maintain maps showing exact locations of underground water networks.', 'https://cejsntpvctcgezrluvql.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/collection-item-images/00000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000001/wiki-cache/f5ffda1db30da69f.svg', 6),
    ('Street Light Foundation Cover', 'Spot round or square metal plates at the base of street light poles, often smaller than manhole covers and flush with the surrounding pavement.', 'Detect a circular metal plate centered beneath a street lamp post base, flush with pavement, typically featuring radial or concentric patterns and bolted connection points.', 'common'::public.item_rarity, 'Street light foundation covers seal underground electrical conduits and can withstand vehicle traffic exceeding 10 tons per axle.', 'https://cejsntpvctcgezrluvql.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/collection-item-images/00000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000001/wiki-cache/f37466da42d10ad6.jpg', 7),
